From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Find STK in the default prefixes

FindSTK looks for Stk.h only in a fixed list of directories, one of
them ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/include/stk. On MSYS2 that is /ucrt64/...,
which CMake reads as a path on the current drive, so STK is never found
and the Mallets instrument is left out. Search the default prefixes for
an stk/ subdirectory too.

Upstream: not submitted
---
 cmake/modules/FindSTK.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/modules/FindSTK.cmake b/cmake/modules/FindSTK.cmake
index 6c2f16d..382774d 100644
--- a/cmake/modules/FindSTK.cmake
+++ b/cmake/modules/FindSTK.cmake
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-FIND_PATH(STK_INCLUDE_DIR Stk.h /usr/include/stk /usr/local/include/stk ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/include/stk ${CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH}/include/stk)
+FIND_PATH(STK_INCLUDE_DIR Stk.h PATHS /usr/include/stk /usr/local/include/stk ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/include/stk ${CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH}/include/stk PATH_SUFFIXES stk)
 
 FIND_LIBRARY(STK_LIBRARY NAMES stk PATH /usr/lib /usr/local/lib ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/lib ${CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH}/lib) 
 
